<div class="post">
	 <h3 class="storytitle" id="post-103"><a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?p=103" rel="bookmark">Conventions and the Store</a></h3>
	<div class="meta">Filed under: <a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=4" title="View all posts in Conventions" rel="category">Conventions</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=2" title="View all posts in Jewelry" rel="category">Jewelry</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=57" title="View all posts in New York" rel="category">New York</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=10" title="View all posts in School" rel="category">School</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=36" title="View all posts in Updates" rel="category">Updates</a> &#8212; Nuri at 2:49 pm on Thursday, June 18, 2009  </div>
	
	<div class="storycontent">
		<p>I am caught up from May conventions. Thank you everyone who came out and visited at <strong><u><a href="http://www.animazement.org">Animazement</a></u></strong> and <strong><u><a href="http://www.concarolinas.org">ConCarolinas</a></u></strong>! I have 2 more conventions planned for July, so take a look at the schedule page if you are interested in seeing my work in person.</p>
<p>I would like to <strong>REMIND</strong> everyone who purchased anything from me that when you email me, you need to be able to receive the reply! <strong>Add my address to your whitelist</strong>. I have replied to a few people that did not respond, so I&#8217;m not sure if my email was blocked by a spam filter. I will try to reach you through 2 email addresses, and if I don&#8217;t hear from you after that then I will let it go. A good alternative to this is to send me a &#8220;convo&#8221; on Etsy; that gets around the problem of email spam filtering.</p>
<p>Also, I&#8217;ve gotten the <strong><u><a href="http://candycornstudios.etsy.com">store</a></u></strong> back up to speed and am listing some new items! Keep an eye on it since I will be updating nearly every day.</p>
<p>I will be moving to New York on July 4, so things will be busy around here. Custom requests will have to wait until after then, as will shirt listings and purchases. The shirts are already packed up in boxes. After I finish moving, there will be approximately a week before Otakon, and then another two weeks before ConnectiCon. That&#8217;s the end of con season for me, so store listings will pick up heavily in August. As always, I&#8217;ll post here when I deactivate the store for a convention or when I do a major update.</p>
<p>Thanks again everybody!</p>
	</div>
	
	<div class="feedback">
                        <a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?p=103#respond" title="Comment on Conventions and the Store">Comments (0)</a>	</div>
	
