<div class="post">
	 <h3 class="storytitle" id="post-100"><a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?p=100" rel="bookmark">Store going to Vacation mode on May 20</a></h3>
	<div class="meta">Filed under: <a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=12" title="View all posts in Charlotte" rel="category">Charlotte</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=4" title="View all posts in Conventions" rel="category">Conventions</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=51" title="View all posts in Geekery" rel="category">Geekery</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=2" title="View all posts in Jewelry" rel="category">Jewelry</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=36" title="View all posts in Updates" rel="category">Updates</a> &#8212; Nuri at 12:35 pm on Friday, May 15, 2009  </div>
	
	<div class="storycontent">
		<p>Attention Candy Corn Shoppers! The Etsy store (yes, the store link on this page goes there) will be rendered inactive on Wednesday, May 20 and will return after June 1. If there is something you want from the store, I highly recommend you purchase it before then. Here&#8217;s why:</p>
<p>Every single item in my stock is going to be for sale at <a href="http://www.animazement.org">Animazement</a> (in Raleigh, NC) over Memorial Day weekend. Anything left after Animazement will be going to <a href="http://www.concarolinas.org/">Con Carolinas</a> (in Charlotte, NC) the following weekend. This INCLUDES all items listed in the Etsy store. I don&#8217;t want anyone purchasing an item from the online store only to find out that it has been sold at the convention, so I will put my Etsy store on Vacation mode and TAKE DOWN all listings for items that were sold at the con before re-activating the store. </p>
<p>I have considerably more stock than I have listed on Etsy, so more items will be available in the Etsy store shortly after it is reactivated. However, they may not be the same ones that are there now, and I don&#8217;t like to make exact duplicates of items. Consider this your warning: If you&#8217;re considering something in the store, try to decide before May 20. Otherwise you may lose the opportunity!</p>
<p>I&#8217;m very excited about Animazement&#8230;I hope to see a bunch of you there!</p>
	</div>
	
	<div class="feedback">
                        <a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?p=100#respond" title="Comment on Store going to Vacation mode on May 20">Comments (0)</a>	</div>
	
