</div>



	
<div class="post">
	 <h3 class="storytitle" id="post-96"><a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?p=96" rel="bookmark">Star Trek! (no spoilers)</a></h3>
	<div class="meta">Filed under: <a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=51" title="View all posts in Geekery" rel="category">Geekery</a> &#8212; Nuri at 11:35 am on Monday, May 11, 2009  </div>
	
	<div class="storycontent">
		<p><strong>I went to see the new Trek movie this weekend.</strong> I must say that I was impressed.</p>
<p>After seeing the trailers, I expected the movie to be enjoyable, but not great. I was happily surprised that I enjoyed the movie immensely and was not at all struck by cheesiness or camp. (Some of my friends had been calling it very cheesy, in a good way.) I personally felt the actors did a great job of getting into character. One of my friends compared it to <strong>Serenity</strong>. I wouldn&#8217;t go quite that far, but it did have its moments. I don&#8217;t think it had the plot strength of Serenity, but it did have almost that level of dialogue and excitement.</p>
<p>In particular, the backstory at the front end of the movie was a great addition that I didn&#8217;t expect. There was just enough setup to the story that you could connect with the characters. This movie is clearly a character-driven story and not a plot-driven story, so don&#8217;t expect an earth-shattering plot. Go see it for the characters, not for an amazing story.</p>
<p><strong>Regarding canon</strong>, I personally have no ill-will toward a director who messes with canon, <em>provided</em> he/she lets us know well ahead of time that they are doing it. Abrams very clearly stated that he was departing from canon, so <strong>anyone who doesn&#8217;t want to see a departure shouldn&#8217;t go see this movie</strong>. There were a few times during the movie that my brain had to do a little adjusting, but most of the time it was easy enough that it didn&#8217;t impact my enjoyment.</p>
<p>Overall, <strong>I heartily recommend you go see this movie</strong> if you haven&#8217;t already. Even if you have, it&#8217;s worth going back to see again!</p>
	</div>
	
	<div class="feedback">
                        <a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?p=96#respond" title="Comment on Star Trek! (no spoilers)">Comments (0)</a>	</div>
	
