<div class="post">
	 <h3 class="storytitle" id="post-65"><a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?p=65" rel="bookmark">New Dice!</a></h3>
	<div class="meta">Filed under: <a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=4" title="View all posts in Conventions" rel="category">Conventions</a>,<a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?cat=2" title="View all posts in Jewelry" rel="category">Jewelry</a> &#8212; Nuri at 10:47 am on Tuesday, April 14, 2009  </div>
	
	<div class="storycontent">
		<p>My order from <a href="http://www.koplowgames.com">Koplow</a> arrived in the mail! I&#8217;m excited to start making new jewelry again. Just put in a huge order for new beads and supplies from <a href="http://www.firemountaingems.com/">Fire Mountain Gems</a>, so I&#8217;ll be able to play with all kinds of colors and designs that I couldn&#8217;t make before. Right now I&#8217;m just getting all the dice prepped and the holes drilled so that when the beads come in I&#8217;ll be ready to get started right away.</p>
<p>Check out all the yummy goodies!</p>
<p><img src="http://www.candycornstudios.com/pics/dice2.jpg"></p>
<p>And here they are all spread out:</p>
<p><img src="http://www.candycornstudios.com/pics/dice1.jpg"></p>
<p>Still waiting for <a href="http://www.chessex.com/">Chessex</a> to get my wholesale account application so I can get some dice from them, too. I hope it gets done in time for me to get some more Chessex dice for <a href="http://www.animazement.org">Animazement</a>! I still have quite a few of the Chessex dice I picked up at <a href="http://www.dragoncon.org/">Dragon*con</a> last year, so at least I will have some of the elaborate pretties if all else fails. For now&#8230;grinding, drilling, scraping plastic off the bit&#8230;so glad I have a nice dust mask from the lab!</p>
	</div>
	
	<div class="feedback">
                        <a href="http://www.candycornstudios.com/?p=65#respond" title="Comment on New Dice!">Comments (0)</a>	</div>
	
	<!--
	<rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
